- The change in control occurs when either Party to this Agreement enters into a merger, consolidation, stock sale or transfer of assets that results in the subject Party retaining title ownership over properties and assets representing more than fifty percent (50%) of its consolidated total assets.
- If such an acquisition or change of control happens:
  - At least fifty percent (50%) of the members of the Board of Directors or similar governing body must have been from the same entity immediately prior to the transaction;
  - The Successor must retain substantially the same proportion of voting power as the original party; 
  - The success of at least fifty percent (50%) of the operating income for the most recent fiscal period should be maintained.
